<h1
id="multi-species-occupancy-models-with-correlated-species-occurrences">Multi-species
Occupancy Models with Correlated Species Occurrences</h1>
<p>This repository contains source code for</p>
<ol type="1">
<li><p>simulating data based on the assumptions of a multivariate probit
occupancy model with correlated species occurrences</p></li>
<li><p>fitting the multi-species occupancy model and its latent-factor
approximation to the simulated data</p></li>
<li><p>fitting a multivariate probit regression model to the matrix of
simulated species occurrences</p></li>
<li><p>fitting the multi-species occupancy model to the Tibetan Plateau
data</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 id="list-of-directories">List of Directories:</h2>
<ul>
<li><p><em>data</em> - contains the Tibetan Plateau data</p></li>
<li><p><em>docs</em> - contains a complete description of the model and
supplements</p></li>
<li><p><em>src</em> - contains source code for simulating data and for
fitting models (code includes R and Julia languages)</p></li>
<li><p><em>tests</em> - contains Julia code for analysis of data sets
(simulated or real)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="publications">Publications:</h2>
<p><a href="https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210x.70168">Dorazio, Li, Xiao,
and Kachel (2025) An evaluation of multi-species occupancy models with
correlated species occurrences. Methods in Ecology and Evolution 16:
2681-2693.</a></p>
<p>The original MCMC algorithm used to fit the multivariate probit (MP)
occupancy model (<em>Appendix S1</em>), included updates of
Z<sub>i,j</sub> that failed to properly account for the correlations in
occurrence between species. The corrected MCMC algorithm is described
in</p>
<p><a href="https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210x.70246">Dorazio, Li, Xiao,
and Kachel (2026) Correction to `An evaluation of multi-species
occupancy models with correlated species occurrences’. Methods in
Ecology and Evolution 17: 1007-1008.</a></p>
<p><em>AppendixS1_correctedMCMC.pdf</em></p>
<h2 id="required-r-packages">Required R packages</h2>
<p><code>mvtnorm, tmvtnorm, msm, MASS, clusterGeneration, mcmcse, coda, rjags</code></p>
<h2 id="required-julia-packages">Required Julia packages</h2>
<p><code>StatsBase, Distributions, Random, Missings, LinearAlgebra, GLM, Optim, ForwardDiff, LogDensityProblems, ADTypes, logDensityProblemsAD, AdvancedHMC, DelimitedFiles, MCMCChains, StatsPlots, DataFrames, CSV, TimerOutputs, Dates</code></p>
